-- title:
--   Decomposition order at a supersingular point equals #Aut(E,C)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$ (`hq`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `hA`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. The finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` is required by `hW` to consist exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`, and $s \in W$ is one of them. The inclusion `hle` asserts that the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ is contained in `fieldBar q M'`, the level-$H$ field at level $q^2M'$. The datum $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the base-changed function field together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing the residue map of $A$ on constants, satisfying the scaling-normalisation and degree- and order-preservation clauses of that structure; `hR₀` pins $R_0$ down on Laurent series with coefficients in $A$: for every $y \in$ `LaurentSeries A` whose image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   The constant field data consist of an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`); write $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation ring of $k_0$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, henselian, and with algebraically closed residue field, and `hκ` states that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0 \cap A$.
--
--   Auxiliary level data: a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`), an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hζ₀`), and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖtA`, `hϖt`). Further, $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`), $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ cut out by $A$ (`hAb`), and $\varpi_b$ a non-zero generator of its maximal ideal (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`). A second prime $\ell'$ satisfies $3 \le \ell'$, $\ell' \ne q$, $\ell' \nmid M'$ (`hℓ'3`, `hℓ'q`, `hℓ'M`), the tameness hypothesis `htame` makes $\ell'(\ell'^2-1)$ a unit of $A_0$, and $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`).
--
--   The rigid-level field is an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of `LaurentSeries k₀` over $k_0$, required by `hKℓ` to be the base change to $k_0$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ') M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell')^\times$; $K_\ell$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$. The element $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ has Laurent expansion the image of $jq$ under `coeffEmb k₀` (`hjℓ`) and is non-zero. The element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$ maps to $\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`). Here `chartAlgFin A₀ K_ℓ jℓ` denotes the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ of elements integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, the $j$-finite chart.
--
--   The point of the chart is a maximal ideal $y$ of `chartAlgFin A₀ K_ℓ jℓ` (`hy`) containing $\pi_0$ (`hϖy`), supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra with kernel $y$, the image $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`, the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero $q$-torsion point. The hypothesis `hover` says that $y$ lies over $s$: for every $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose base change lies in `R₀.integers`, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $jq$ does, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$, the difference between the element of the chart algebra determined by the $\ell'$-fold $q$-expansion of $g$ and the constant $c$ lies in $y$. The hypothesis `hOrbit` states transitivity of the level action on such points: every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra which contains $\pi_0$ and satisfies the same lying-over condition is of the form described by some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and some $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ (q*ℓ') ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M')` — that is, $\tau$ realises on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ the substitution by `conjElemN (q*ℓ') γ⁻¹`, under any embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$ — such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra and $b \in y \iff \tau b \in y'$.
--
--   The supersingular component is given by an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t$ of $K_\ell$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` is a conjunction of clauses, summarised here: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$ and $K_\ell$ is the field of fractions of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$ and $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is the localisation of $B_t$ at its maximal ideal, and cuts out $y$ on the chart algebra; for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa_0$ of $A_0$ there is a surjection $\rho$ of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ₀`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $\kappa_0[X_0,X_1]$-power-free polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) κ₀` by the Drinfeld equation) with kernel $B_t \cap \mathfrak{m}_{W_t}$, inducing the residue map on constants and equivariant for level automorphisms: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$ there is a unit $c$ of $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det(g) c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau =$ `hAction` of that pair composed with $\rho$, with $c \ne 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$, and with the same scalar $c$ realised by a pair with trivial matrix part by some $\gamma' \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and some level automorphism $\tau'$ preserving $W_t$ (the linked-scalars clause); $B_t$ is stable under level automorphisms for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is obtained from $B_t \cap \mathfrak{m}_{W_t}$ by such a level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_t}$ after all such translations is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   The integer in question is $n$ with $1 \le n$ (`hn1`) and $n \mid q+1$ (`hnq`), accompanied by: $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`, `hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`); an integer $m \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t'$ times a unit of $A_0$ (`hm1`, `hm`); an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ with $\zeta_c^n = 1$ and $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζc`, `hζcprim`); and a finset `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. The hypothesis `hR7` is again a conjunction of clauses, summarised here: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while $\tau_0^k$ moves some element of $B_t$ for $0 < k < n$, and every level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with some $\tau_0^k$, $k < n$; `ends` has $q+1$ members, is permuted by the level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$, forms a single orbit under them, each member is preserved by $\tau_0$, and distinct members are separated by an element which is a unit in one and not in the other; each $O \in$ `ends` is contained in $W_t$, is a noetherian local ring containing the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ exactly in $A_0$, has every element congruent to a constant, and admits a crossing description: $\pi_0 \in O$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$ and a unit $u$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion of $A_0$ at $\pi_0^m$ which is the identity on constants and carries $c_x, c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$ and $V$, with $c_y$ in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_t}$ and $c_x$ outside it, transporting $\tau_0$ to an automorphism $\theta_0$ acting on $U$ and $V$ by $\zeta_c$ and its inverse $\zeta_c'$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal; together with a transverse valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ containing $O$ and the chart algebra, meeting $k_0$ in $A_0$, discretely valued with uniformiser $\pi_0$, carrying a residually independent element $t$, with $c_x$ in and $c_y$ outside its maximal ideal, and cutting out a condition comparable with $y$ on the chart algebra; and a finite-type $A_0$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $B_t \cap O$, stable under level automorphisms with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, whose elements are regular wherever $j_\ell$ is and whose localisation is $O$. A final clause of `hR7` states that any valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ which meets $k_0$ in $A_0$, contains the chart algebra and whose maximal ideal contracts to a set containing $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the members of `ends`. The hypothesis `hR5d` states that a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ on the chart algebra also preserves $W_t$.
--
--   Finally, $E$ is an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` and `Cyc` is a cyclic subgroup of $E(\kappa)$ of cardinality $M'$ (`hcyc`, `hcardCyc`), and `hP` requires the valuation subring of the place $s$ to be the contraction, along the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` into the full modular function field over $\kappa$, of the valuation subring of the moduli place `moduliPlace κ M' E Cyc` attached to the pair $(E, \mathrm{Cyc})$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the single equality
--   $$n = \#\{\iota : E(\kappa) \to E(\kappa) \ \text{additive}\ \mid\ \iota \in \mathrm{rationalHomSet}(\kappa, E, E),\ \exists\, \iota' \in \mathrm{rationalHomSet}(\kappa, E, E) \text{ with } \iota' \circ \iota = \mathrm{id} = \iota \circ \iota',\ \iota(\mathrm{Cyc}) = \mathrm{Cyc}\},$$
--   where [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalHomSet κ E E`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L28) is the set of additive endomorphisms which are either zero or rationally represented in the sense of the predicate `IsRationallyRepresented`, and the cardinality is that of the subtype of such $\iota$. Thus $n$ is the order of the group of automorphisms of $E$ over $\kappa$ preserving the cyclic subgroup `Cyc`.
--
--   This is the order count identifying the integer $n$ — the order of the cyclic group through which the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ that stabilise the exceptional (Drinfeld) component act on it — with the order of $\operatorname{Aut}(E, C)$ for the pair of an elliptic curve and a cyclic subgroup of order $M'$ over the residue field whose moduli place is the chosen supersingular place $s$. It is obtained from the stabiliser description of the decomposition group together with the count of automorphisms fixing the corresponding moduli point, and it feeds the comparison of the decomposition order with twice the width character of the place.
